# Campus scene digitized from docs/sketchup_top.png
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Coordinates are half-scale pixels from the SketchUp top-down screenshot
# (1920x970 -> 960x485). Origin top-left, +y downward.
#
# Record formats:
#   CANVAS   width height
#   VIEWPORT xmin ymin xmax ymax
#   PAD      name  x1 y1 x2 y2 ...     # white site pad
#   LAWN     name  x1 y1 x2 y2 ...     # green planters / grass
#   PARKING  name  x1 y1 x2 y2 ...     # gray plaza
#   BUILDING name  x1 y1 x2 y2 ...     # footprint polygon
#   ROAD     name  x0 y0 x1 y1 x2 y2 x3 y3 [w]   # cubic Bezier + width
#   TREE     name  x y radius
#   CAR      name  x y length width angle
#
# How to add a ROAD (cubic Bezier path)
#   ROAD  name  x0 y0  x1 y1  x2 y2  x3 y3  [width]
#   - (x0,y0) start and (x3,y3) end: the road passes exactly through these.
#   - (x1,y1) and (x2,y2) are control "handles": the road leaves the start
#     heading toward P1 and arrives at the end coming from P2. Pull a handle
#     farther away for a rounder bend; put both on the start-end line for a
#     straight road.
#   - width is in scene pixels (default thickness is used if omitted).
#   Example: a path that leaves (400,420) heading up, bows right, and ends at
#   (500,250):
#     ROAD  my_path  400 420  430 340  520 340  500 250  8
#   Tips: roads are painted BEFORE parking/buildings, so a road drawn over a
#   PARKING plaza or BUILDING is hidden. Keep roads on the PAD (white) or lawn
#   and read coordinates off docs/sketchup_top.png (half scale).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

CANVAS   960 485

# Zoom window over the E-building and the plaza edge. 320 x 161.67 has the
# same aspect as the 960 x 485 canvas, so the zoom is a uniform 3x (no
# stretching). Edges deliberately cut the E's top wing, the pad and a car.
VIEWPORT 190 190 510 351.67

# White site pad (from SketchUp)
PAD      site_pad    454.0 33.5  166.5 197.5  200.0 303.0  275.5 425.0  525.0 425.0  525.0 290.0

# Gray paved plaza (left of the building)
PARKING  plaza       166.5 197.0  201.5 306.5  258.5 398.0  297.0 425.0  401.0 425.0  308.0 283.0  312.0 260.5  243.0 149.5

# Green planter islands (capsule polygons traced from the SketchUp ovals)
LAWN     planter_n   221.5 199.5  266.0 294.5  274.0 296.5  276.5 289.5  230.5 201.5
LAWN     planter_s   283.0 316.5  281.0 323.0  316.0 390.5  326.5 396.5  328.5 390.0  291.0 318.0

# E-shaped building footprint (outer silhouette traced from SketchUp).
# Corners are intersections of straight lines least-squares fitted to the
# outline pixels of each SketchUp edge, then halved and rounded to 0.5 px.
# Order: top tab -> left spine (with the small entrance step) -> bottom arm
# -> middle arm -> top arm -> back to the tab. Concave notches between the
# arms are handled by the even-odd scanline fill.
BUILDING e_bldg      379.5 139.5  348.5 155.5  361.0 179.0  302.5 210.0  333.5 269.5  325.5 272.5  336.0 292.0  342.5 288.5  370.5 341.0  478.0 285.0  468.0 267.0  384.0 310.5  365.5 274.0  446.0 231.5  433.5 206.5  352.0 248.5  339.5 223.5  423.0 180.5  409.0 153.0  391.0 162.0

# Curved access path (cubic Bezier). Leaves the plaza's south end, bows around
# the south tip of the E-building and ends east of it, so the bend is clearly
# visible on the white pad (roads sit under the plaza/building in paint order).
ROAD     access      410 420  440 350  520 340  495 250   8

# Second path: from the plaza's north edge, arcing over the top of the building
# to the east side of the pad.
ROAD     north_walk  265 175  310 110  430 100  470 150   6

# Symbolic trees near the site (2D canopy symbols — design decision)
# Placed on the grass just outside the pad edges, clear of the black road
# band on the left of the SketchUp view.
TREE     t1   205 158  12
TREE     t2   515 140  13
TREE     t3   552 330  11
TREE     t4   148 300  10

# Cars parked nose-in to the painted stalls on the building side of the
# plaza (stall lines at SketchUp y ~ 420-507 full scale). Stalls are ~14 px
# deep and ~7 px wide here, so cars are 12 x 5.5 with small angle jitter;
# stall 2 and 5 are left empty.
CAR      c1  276.0 213.5  12 5.5   0
CAR      c2  285.0 228.0  12 5.5  -3
CAR      c3  290.0 236.5  12 5.5   2
CAR      c4  298.5 250.0  12 5.5   0
